Ladybird picks a web font’s decoder from the signature of its data,
and never from the response’s Content-Type. Gecko does the same: Its
gfxUserFontEntry::SanitizeOpenTypeData() takes the type from
gfxFontUtils::DetermineFontDataType(), which reads the data. Blink’s
DecodeFontWithIft() hands the data to OTS, whose OTSContext::Process()
tells WOFF, WOFF2, collections and sfnt data apart by their signature.
And WebKit’s CachedFont calls convertWOFFToSfntIfNecessary(), which
converts the data only if isWOFF() finds the WOFF signature in it.
